{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf","id":1556500,"title":"Minotaur as an enemy faction in Werewolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-11T21:44:38-08:00","id":1556500,"title":"Minotaur as an enemy faction in Werewolf","content":"As people know, Minotaur is the Incarna patron of the Skin Dancers. Although the Skin Dancers were introduced earlier, I believe the first mention of Minotaur himself is from 1995\u2019s Outcasts sourcebook where he is given the epitaph <i>That-Which-Howls-In-The-Forests</i>. He\u2019s since been developed a little bit more in Players Guide to Garou and some of the W20 material.<br /> <br /> I think Minotaur has potential to become something more than just the patron of the Skin Dancers. Note that when I describe this as a faction, I don\u2019t mean the Minotaur Incarna is leading or controlling some kind of conspiracy or army. Just that Minotaur can be the source of additional antagonists than just the Skin Dancers, and that these different groups may or may not cooperate with each other locally.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll be using this thread to explore some ideas I\u2019ve been having. More to come.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T22:16:06-08:00","id":1556503,"title":"","content":"It definitely sounds like a good Mood-Shift for a story. It'd definitely require a Storyteller that knows how to prevent Jagglings and Gafflings from overcrowding the area, so Minotaur's influence in the area can diminish (and get forced out).<br /> <br /> I'm all ears. Who are the members of the Skin Dancer pack? Is it only 2 or 3 members who decide that they're up to shenanigans, or are there more?<br /> <br /> Normally they don't work with Black Spiral Dancers, but is one in their vicinity (hoping to snatch the knowledge of the Rite of Rebirth)? If no = ok. If yes = Another character.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of questions that can by machine-gunn'd here, but I don't want to overwhelm you. I want to let you cook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28838-dafrontlinespecter","name":"DaFrontlineSpecter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T22:56:59-08:00","id":1556505,"title":"","content":"He is full of possibilities and could be in the <i>Big Leagues </i>so to speak<br /> <br /> At his core, he is the embodiment of the man that becomes the beast, the sentient being who craves animalistic power. So, his servants are gravitate toward these things - this a bit set him up to be the de facto ally of the Patriarch (who according the Black Furies, the Incarna of jealous men - explaining their enmity with him) a facet of the Weaver, representing her <i>Seed of Dogma</i>.<br /> But he is not Corrupt (juts corrupt...ish) nor served the Wyrm - in Skinner it is even possible to cleanse him - he could represent something ugly that the Garou noit really want to face in themselves or in the world to give some depth to the story. Breaking that Garou indoctrination and brainwashing showing Cubs and young werewolves the World is not <i>that </i>black and white could be fun - and would make him extremly dangerous to the whole<br /> <br /> As a full blown enemy his rivalry against Pegasus (and by extension the Black Furies) is literally legendary witch <i><b>could</b></i> set him up as a spiritual &quot;mastermind&quot; behind several events - like the one who engineered the Metamorphic Plague (especially fun if it was with the assistance of the Wyld)<br /> Just because you are the embodiment of the man that becomes the beast, the sentient being who craves animalistic power not necesarilly means you are dumb; you can be both like that and smart; Wilson Fisk, the King Pin, Bane (especially the Ultimate kind) are both good examples, but even from a certaibn point of view Vandal Savage or Kraven the Hunter<br /> And of course that little rivalry put him in a sweet spot to ally himself or lend a hand to Garou... who are not that keen about the Black Furies - e.g. the Get of Fenris; Minutaur and the Get could find themselves on the same side as strange bedfellows and even the Red Talons could see probably the &quot;merits&quot; what he could say. Or do. Or what a Garou should be - the Old Wolf of the Woods (who probably was the Tallons or not the whole Garou race original racial totem) would even support this idea<br /> <br /> You could meld splats and he really could be the Minotaur, an Apis/Abomination who ascended like Hakaken and Number Two and became an Incarna<br /> If he was an Apis who became an Incarna his whole plot could be a very long revenge for what happened with his people<br /> Or he once was a noble and wise Totem, the racial patron of the Apis just when his people died by tooth and claws he got so pissed, he became Minotaur<br /> <br /> He is a treasuretrove of opportunities\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 12-12-2025, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T10:06:51-08:00","id":1556519,"title":"","content":"Before I get to the actual entities involved in this faction, I want to address the concept of the Minotaur and its possible ties to the actual Greek legend of the minotaur.<br /> <br /> \u201cMinotaur\u201d as a concept is something that crops up in other places in the World of Darkness. There's both Werewolf and Vampire mentions (and I believe Mage as well). The first Children of Gaia tribebook mentions Crete and seeing the last of the noble Moon-bulls/Minotaurs. It also states that once Minoan Crete was a Gaian centered civilization, but later became corrupt and needed to be destroyed. Later editions of Werewolf introduced the concept of the Last Apis reappearing in Crete that went berserk and became part of the minotaur legend.<br /> <br /> We also have repeated mentions of Minoan Crete in Vampire. The revised Toreador Clanbook said the Minotaur (Asterion) is a childe of the clan founder who entered wassail and was imprisoned in the labyrinth. Interestingly, while that sourcebook said that Toreador refused to embrace Minos, Asterion\u2019s father, we actually know that there was a fourth generation Toreador named Minos who embraced Helena. So is that Minos not THE Minos? Or do we just accept that the in character knowledge we're provided is often incomplete or wrong. I am leaning towards the latter. For our purposes, we just know that the Toreador clan founder was active on Crete - probably fairly early or in the middle of Minoan Civilization (possibly around 2000 BC).<br /> <br /> We also know that at some point the Baali arrived in Minoan Crete from The Dark Ages Companion for Vampire: the Dark Ages. Although no mention of a minotaur is made there, they do make references to using a labyrinth beneath Knossos, that inhuman things dwelled there, and that they used various occult powers during this time. I assume that at some point the Toreador antediluvian left, and the Baali creeped in afterwards. We are also told that it was mortal heroes killing deformed Baali ghouls that was the basis of the Theseus legend. When other vampires learned of the Baali activities there, the Setites worked magic to create the Thera/Santorini volcanic eruption (which we know was around 1600 BC) which caused the Knossos palace to collapse, the Baali labyrinth to collapse, and fires to erupt which incinerated most of the Baali.<br /> <br /> We can easily tie these things together. Very early Minoan Crete (before the arrival of Toreador) was Gaian centered, perhaps because of the presence of earlier Apis and continued survival of people descended from Apis kinfolk (regardless of whether they counted as actual kinfolk by that point). That began to chance when Toreador arrived, but definitely changed when the Baali arrived and introduced their dark magics and worship of evil things.<br /> <br /> Maybe the thing that drove the Last Apis mad was seeing the descendants of the Apis kinfolk being manipulated and embraced by vampires. Perhaps the spirit of \u201cthe beast in man\u201d was somehow involved in his degeneration into a mindless beast. References to the labyrinth can mean there was some kind of connection to the labyrinth the Garou know best - the Black Spiral found in Malfeas. The Minotaur Incarna need only be one spirit that the Baali managed to successfully contact and perhaps sacrifice to. The exact nature of this relationship can be left to the ST. Maybe this was the place and time when the spirit became partially corrupted. Or it was first formed as a result of the activity here, or perhaps ascended from mere jaggling to its own Incarna status.<br /> <br /> The minotaur of legend might have been the Last Apis, a deformed ghoul, a 4th generation vampire in Wassail, some combination (a ghouled Last Apis or even Abomination?), or perhaps multiple stories involving different creatures which we're eventually combined into one legend. STs can determine whatever they like best. I actually think this is the least important thing to consider, but some STs will no doubt have strong opinions.<br /> <br /> But does this actually provide us anything? Or is this just archaeology and pointless connecting different canons together? I do think a high level perspective does offer some benefits. YMMV.<br /> <br /> I wouldn\u2019t want to tie current vampires into the Minotaur Incarna, and I certainly don\u2019t want him directly involved with the Baali. But I have no problem with the idea that he could have been a spirit some Baali were once in contact with, and thus was an important spirit the corrupted Minoans were in contact with.<br /> <br /> References to the \u201cfall\u201d or corruption of Minoan Crete has been around in the game since the first Children of Gaia sourcebook. So tying Minotaur Incarna in some way to the fall of an originally Gaian Great Goddess religion/civilaztion practiced in Minoan Crete (perhaps under the original guidance of the Apis) into a corrupted civilization that had to be destroyed would provide some real heritage and meance to the spirit. It also provides some good plot hooks for other things in later eras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T10:15:30-08:00","id":1556520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaFrontlineSpecter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556503#post1556503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm all ears. Who are the members of the Skin Dancer pack? Is it only 2 or 3 members who decide that they're up to shenanigans, or are there more?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the purpose of this thread, I am not talking one specific scenario. It's more about tools STs can use to develop the idea in their own chronicles regardless of any time or place. The numbers or personalities of one or more Skin Dancer packs isn't important. Of course, if STs decide to apply anything to their own unique chronicles, they'll have to decide on things like that.<br /> <br /> While Skin Dancers were originally presented as just another evil group fallen to the Wyrm, later sourcebooks tried to present a more nuanced version with packs ranging from fully Wyrm corrupted to those trying to follow the Litany on their own, and Minotaur being somewhat corrupted, but not entirely fallen to the Wyrm. So I will be trying to thread that needle myself. Different STs will have different visions of what the minions of Minotaur should be like. Some will want to emphasize their villainy, while others may want to lean more into them being more grey and allow individuals to even be heroic.<br /> <br /> Since I'm more concerned with their use as an enemy faction, I'll be concentrating more as antagonists as opposed to potential allies, but I hope those who want to portray certain members more heroically to still do so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T10:25:32-08:00","id":1556522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556505#post1556505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He is full of possibilities and could be in the <i>Big Leagues </i>so to speak</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there is definitely potential here. I'm going to cover the more obvious, low hanging fruit first, but I also want to talk about potential that is a lot less obvious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556505#post1556505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">he could represent something ugly that the Garou noit really want to face in themselves or in the world to give some depth to the story. Breaking that Garou indoctrination and brainwashing showing Cubs and young werewolves the World is not <i>that </i>black and white could be fun - and would make him extremly dangerous to the whole\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Minotaur as a way for Garou to gain more power is certainly something I want to explore. Certainly Shadow Lords in the Bringers of Light camp could justify themselves getting into some relationship with him because it's just a way to &quot;test&quot; themselves. I also think there is a lot of potential for Minotaur worship among the Man Eaters camp of Bone Gnawers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556505#post1556505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">even from a certaibn point of view Vandal Savage or Kraven the Hunter\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea. Secret concoctions and lore that provide strength and powers (perhaps even longevity) to very masculine, physical hunters is a great idea. Maybe there is even a secret society or hunting lodge of such people. Perfect for hunters who want to test themselves against the most challenging prey, and that prey could even be Garou or other Changing Breeds. It would make an interesting new group of hunters, who of course only see themselves as good guys protecting humanity for these horrible monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T10:34:36-08:00","id":1556523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556519#post1556519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly, while that sourcebook said that Toreador refused to embrace Minos, Asterion\u2019s father, we actually know that there was a fourth generation Toreador named Minos who embraced Helena. So is that Minos not THE Minos?</div> </div> </div> </div>He is<br /> But there are <i>two </i>Toreador Antedulivians<br /> <b>Arikel, the Sculptor</b>, the twin of Malkav (and Malakai) sister of Nahema<br /> And <b>Ishtar the Bull-Dancer</b><br /> I made a detailed essay of them here <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511164-arikel#post1511195\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...el#post1511195</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T10:53:37-08:00","id":1556524,"title":"","content":"I actually think the Baali in this particular story may work well, as participants in this &quot;faction&quot; that don't necessarily understand the thing they're worshiping, but nonetheless turning this worship to evil. There may be individuals who break this mold, of course, and this sub-faction may both manipulate the others, work with them, or come into conflict with them.<br /> <br /> Also, as far as the origin of the legends matter, I think as a semi-corrupted being instead of a fully corrupted one, I think Minotaur would either fight or at least try to resist the dark influences that came. Something Gaian still survives within even if he's now the nearest thing we have to a neutral Incarna.<br /> <br /> There's also a number of interpretations and tidbits about the myth of the Minotaur that may inform this beyond the notion of &quot;man that becomes the beast&quot;:<ul><li>It was possibly originally a Sun God figure;</li> <li>Minos' wife fucking the bull may have been a ritual, a sacred ceremony, possibly linked to said god;</li> <li>It may have been a Brazen Bull, a torture/execution instrument, used on criminals and/or sacrificial victims;</li> <li>Through the Brazen Bull, it may share origin with the myth of Talos;</li> <li>It may have been a god <i>or goddess</i> associated with stars and/or grain;</li> <li>It may have been an interpretation for earthquakes or other geological phenomena from the region.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T12:24:37-08:00","id":1556530,"title":"","content":"What if Asterion the son of Minos was an Apis who was later Embraced by Arikel the Toreador Antediluvian and became an Abomination trapped in Crinos form (or the equivalent for Apis)? That would mesh well with legends indicating that the Minotaur was the son of Minos\u2019s wife and a great white bull. And what if Arikel later changed her mind and Embraced Minos as well? This theory could reconcile all the conflicting lore you mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 12-12-2025, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T12:39:42-08:00","id":1556535,"title":"","content":"Given the legend of Theseus and the Minotaur is one of my particular favourites from Hellenistic mythology (Ever since I realised it was more or less a Bronze Age Bond movie with some extra Ray Harryhausen for spice) so the title of this thread got my attention all on it\u2019s own, but your \u2018archaeology\u2019 just makes the Fall of Minoan Crete sound like a fascinating collision of supernatural elements that could absolutely support it\u2019s own Horror/Fantasy novel.<br /> <br /> As for Minos the Cainite, my personal inclination is to make him A Minos who insists that he\u2019s THE Minos (If only because this allows us to put the notion of \u2018Minos\u2019 being a hereditary title, like \u2018Pharaoh\u2019 into the mix) and may even be telling the truth.<br /> <br /> One last element to consider: Theseus, the legendary slayer of the Minotaur, was famously associated with an Amazon (His first Queen, Hippolyta) but he\u2019s somewhat less famously associated with the abduction of a very young Helen of Troy.<br /> <br /> Given both these elements have strong World of Darkness associations (and that Theseus himself was said to have been a \u2018demigod\u2019) one suspects that the WoD Theseus must have led an interesting life \u2026 and possibly an interesting afterlife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T15:34:08-08:00","id":1556539,"title":"","content":"So, we have the Incarna &quot;Minotaur&quot; (which would be the totem - I think), and then we have aspects of &quot;Minotaur&quot; in both the Jaggling and Gaffling sense (because that'd be how Umbrood roll).<br /> Oh Lord.<br /> We're going to be cooking for a while. lol<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm overthinking this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28838-dafrontlinespecter","name":"DaFrontlineSpecter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-12T17:47:24-08:00","id":1556545,"title":"","content":"Something that came up in my (ancient) thread about PENTEX was the possible history and evolution of Slaughterhouse Video, including the idea that whatever force was behind them could conceivably go back to the Creten Minotaur as one of the earliest iterations of the ritual from The Cabin in the Woods. Basically, you have 14 attractive young people trapped in an isolated location they can't leave so that they can be hunted and killed by a faceless brute, i.e. a slasher film. <br /> Taking <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a>'s suggestions about The Man Who Becomes the Beast, you have the idea of that minotaur perhaps being a man in a bull-head mask using a Wyrm-tainted form of shamanism to channel the power of the beast, offering the lives of his victims to the spirit (That Which Howls in the Forests). And this sort of thing could carry on down the centuries in various new forms. At least one of which would be The Most Dangerous Game trope (including the Kraven the Hunter character), as well as the Battle Royale/Hunger Games concept.<br /> Tying that back into Slaughterhouse Video, the earlier slasher genre (from around 1978 to 1984) were all human killers and many could easily inspire a certain type of fan to take up the Man Who Becomes the Beast archetype, including Bane possession by spirits that are part of Minotaur/That Which Howls' brood. As the slasher genre evolves post-84 to focus on supernatural killers, these would become the Gorehounds from the early Werewolf material. There could conceivably be a similar breed even more cunning and deadly. &quot;Demons Who Make Trophies of Men&quot; (or Garou) if you will.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T10:08:05-08:00","id":1556561,"title":"","content":"I'm excited that there's already so many comments and excellent ideas.<br /> <br /> A good first step is to consider what other spirits may make up Minotaur's brood. The W20 corebook suggests Minotaur\u2019s brood consists of some corrupted spirits, some Banes, and spirits not associated with Gaia. As others have said, Minotaur is the Incarna of the beast within man, or when man that becomes the beast. He craves animalistic power. He respects strength and has contempt for the weak. He is touched by the taint of the Beast of War, but not wholly corrupted. So were looking at spirits that fit that theme.<br /> <br /> Players Guide to Garou says, \u201cthe Skin Dancers have sought and, in fact, found spirit servants of forgotten or lost totems such as Minotaur.\u201d That definitely leans more into Minotaur not being a Bane simply a spirit that may have once been worshipped by Garou or the Changing Breeds, but was somehow abandoned. Maybe originally it was some kind of war spirit of the Apis that was lost after the War of Rage, and then subsequently tainted because of Baali blasphemies on Crete that evoked the Beast-of-War.<br /> <br /> It is not explained why Minotaur hates and envies Pegasus. However, I hold it is because he views the sacred feminine as weak and contemptible. He doesn\u2019t understand its obvious power. Another possibility is that the Black Furies performed some act either during the War of Rage or against Wyrm corrupted Minoan Crete that purposefully or inadverently violated something sacred to this spirit, and this caused the Minotaur spirit to bear a grudge against Pegasus. Other explanations are possible, and I\u2019d love to hear them.<br /> <br /> I would include corrupted Naturae that have treacherous or ferocious natures (like scorpions, snakes, wolverines, crocodiles, boars, hyenas, certain raptors, big cats, chimpanzees, and others), feral animals (feral pigs, Lost Dogs, Feral Psychagonea and Feral Psychomachiae - I took most of these from Rat's brood in Axis Mundi), some epiphlings (spirits of hate, pain, anger, darkness), corrupted Lunes, spirits of diseases that cause behaviourly aggression (like rabies), and some elementals. This could be a very motley brood, composed of a ragtag and small group of individual jagglings and gafflings that for whatever reason were cut off from their normal allegiances, and came under Minotaur simply for protection (because he\u2019s somewhat of a bully).<br /> <br /> These spirits can teach Gifts to Skin Dancers who take Minotaur as a pack totem, but have also sometimes taught Gifts to Ronin as well.<br /> <br /> For those who want to distinguish between Skin Dancers who are aligned with the Wyrm, and those who attempt to walk a more Gaian pact, then the Banes who teach Gifts may not explicitly be part of Minotaur\u2019s brood, but something else. The Outcasts sourcebook talks about the Puppeteer banes (from Valkenburg Foundation) as being spirit allies because of their past association with Sam Haight. A paragraph later when talking about \u201cconnections have been made with powers answering to Minotaur,\u201d it\u2019s clearly about those Skin Dancers not attempting to destroy Garou society. It\u2019s just an \u201cunassociated spirit\u201d they\u2019ve made contact with.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s possible to join up these two different spirit groups if you want a Minotaur more in thrall to the Wyrm, or if you want a clear separation, align the less hostile Skin Dancers with Minotaur and align the more hostile Skin Dancers with their own Bane allies. It\u2019s also possible that Skin Dancers may not be able to distinguish between the two groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T10:58:08-08:00","id":1556562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556561#post1556561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A good first step is to consider what other spirits may make up Minotaur's brood. The W20 corebook suggests Minotaur\u2019s brood consists of some corrupted spirits, some Banes, and spirits not associated with Gaia.<br /> (...)<br /> These spirits can teach Gifts to Skin Dancers who take Minotaur as a pack totem, but have also sometimes taught Gifts to Ronin as well.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Depends a bit where do you start and what you want to use<br /> When he was introduced Outcasts: a players guide to pariahs Minotaur not really had a &quot;family&quot; nor servants. He was a totem who simply could teach <i>any </i>Gifts to his followers<br /> And sure he was the de facto patron of the Skindancers but it was never truly stated no one else follows him - to be fair the fact he was able to teach literally any gifts? Holly hell was OP with very little downside<br /> A bit questionable - possibly! tainted - Spirit who wants you to hurt the Black Furies? - heck some Tribes hate them out of tradition!<br /> 'kay?<br /> I mean there are <i>literally</i> worse spirits out there, starting with a totem of War, a cannibal spirit associated with ice and cold, Wendigo, but Uktena was borderline Wyrm...ish and Griffin was basically insane<br /> Grandfather Thunder was just the icing on the top<br /> Tick and other &quot;questionable&quot; totems are lingered around too<br /> To be honest Minotaur was not even the top three red flag if you asks me<br /> <br /> Revised toned his power level a bit back and modified him, so Minotaur places his children in contact with spirits that can teach them Gifts, and thus his children can learn most Gifts of Rank Three or lower (at out-of-tribe costs, of course).<br /> But this opened up a VERY interesting possibility<br /> <br /> So lets unpack this<br /> <br /> <b>Version A</b><br /> Minotaur basically <i>knew </i><b>literally </b><u>every</u> Gift you can find - possibly even other Fera's gifts, plenty of overlaps already, and it not said he can't teach you this and that it just said... any gifts<br /> Minotaur - following this - had to be at one point immensly wise to know all the Gifts and to be able not to know them but teach you. This is improtant. Gifts are while called Gifts are tought to you, it is not some unlocked power! You have to court and suck up to a Spirit who will <i>teach</i> it to you, not just hand it over as a ...gift<br /> Minotaur not only had the knowledge, inteligence and wisdom to know these - either inherently or learned them - but had the ability to <i>teach</i><br /> It is damn hard to pass knowledge, to be able to teach someone<br /> These two things - the knowledge of all the gifts and the wisdom to be able to pass them on - I think were a smoking gun, Minotaur was WAY more than he appeared to be - eg. a brutal strengh obsessed barbarian<br /> But kinda fits in to the fallen Apis totem/ascended Apis theme<br /> And okay, sure he became a bit brutish, but still retained enough of his olders self to be able to pull of what he provided (not like Green Dragon who fall hard for example)<br /> <br /> <b>Version B</b><br /> Minotaur, despite his very bad nature and behavior, reputation and all... still have a connection in the spirit world so immense, it would Weaver's web to shame<br /> Not only knowing what spirits could be help and place contact with those spirits his followers, but those spirits - who are not necesarily his servants - are obliged to teach the servants of Minotaur<br /> This makes him basically the Raymond &quot;Red&quot; Reddington from the Blacklist of the Spirit Wold - and to be fair imagining that scenario where Minotaur ended up in that situation is kinda cool and full of so many possibilities it makes my head spin<br /> And also supports basically the same what Version A presented: Minotaur is way more than he seems<br /> <br /> Either way, Minotaur could present a very interesting part of any story<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556561#post1556561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not explained why Minotaur hates and envies Pegasus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pegasus was originally created to keep the Furies in check in their rage against man when they were backed up -patroned by Artemis, the aspect of Luna<br /> Bellerophon and Pegasus had a bit of a rough breakup and HE took them under HIS wings<br /> Pegasus, many forgot, is a male<br /> And he proclaimed that he would never bend knee again before man.<br /> Minotaur who is the embodiment of the man that becomes the beast, the sentient being who craves animalistic power and may or may not have a connection with the Patriarch are basically the antithesis, pollar opposites of each other<br /> Who knows maybe he was behind the events that ended up Bellerophon becomind distant and afraid of his steed... and gelding him (a gelded stalion probably the most shamefull and dispicable thing in Minotaur's eye I think)<br /> If you beilive the version of the story of course<br /> <br /> But there is another possible explanation - and in my humble oppinion it explains better the grudge<br /> The Apocalypse Record mentions that the Black Furies were Minotaur's 'tormentors' - but not explained or detailed what that means<br /> The Black Furies were his tormentors either because they helped to murder the Apis in the War of Rage - and toremented the totem that way - either because Minotaur himself was an Apis and they helped to trap him in the Labyrinth - both are good explanations<br /> A little Baali connection here could be tossed in the mix, The creature known as Cybele was embraced (or re-embraced) in the darkest corridors of the Knossos' Labyrinth, the greatest Baali fortress of its time by Nergal and the Cult of Cybele brought power to women that had been stolen away by men \u2013 sacrifices of both beasts and men were often by castration.<br /> This seems... Balck Furieish... and fits i nthe picture quite nicely (not to mention Petaniqua, Cybele's Child is famous for working with Werewolves who are usually portrayed to be Black Spiral Dancers, but you can easly see two very independent woman even if undead manage to glue with the Blakc Furies)\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 12-13-2025, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T12:12:41-08:00","id":1556566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556561#post1556561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minotaur is the Incarna of the beast within man, or when man that becomes the beast. He craves animalistic power. He respects strength and has contempt for the weak. He is touched by the taint of the Beast of War, but not wholly corrupted. So were looking at spirits that fit that theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be interesting to give him an aspect of (d)evolution: survival of the fittest, but one that does not rely on natural selection. He accepts the Skindancer's way to gain more power through unnatural means and himself represents a model of how more primal essence (beast) can empower more evolved essence (man). The idea of representing a natural process enforced by unnatural means would fit his particular brand of taint, imo. <br /> <br /> This could lead to his brood having a tendency for rapid adaptation through primal mechanisms, such as disease spirits of pathogens with high mutability rate, or even something related to gene spliced organisms. Parasites would be another good fit. A theme to tie him into a more modern playing field could be &quot;reactivation of ancient junk DNA&quot; that plays on Island of Dr Moreau stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T14:09:11-08:00","id":1556568,"title":"","content":"One angle that could be interesting as a possible route to explain the enmity between Pegasus and Minotaur is what I\u2019ll call the Athena Connection.<br /> <br /> (Disclaimer my inspirations for this are some half-remembered sections of Graves &amp; Frazer and the thankless task of trying to justify after the fact what seems from a Doyalist perspective to be White Wolf\u2019s cavalier practices of sprinkling liberally from randomly selected Greek Mythology references onto Black Furies and other Hellenic touching parts of the setting)<br /> <br /> The main things I want to touch on for this is Theseus, Perseus, &amp; Bellerophon (and maybe Orestes tangentially).<br /> <br /> Starting with Theseus. Theseus is interesting because his stories actually have very little relation to Athena proper, despite him nominally being her polity\u2019s most famous hero. There are however several notable female characters that Theseus interacts with I want to note; including Medea, Ariadne, Phaedra, &amp; Helen. The most directly relevant here of course is Ariadne, oft-speculated to allegorically represent some sort of priestess figure who may have been co-opted into the upstart Attican revolt against Cretan power. Ariadne\u2019s betrayal of her father for Theseus and then subsequent betrayal by Theseus is something I want to note in particular (in the first part taking the role of Athena as comprador I\u2019ll describe later on and in the second part taking the role of victimized priestess figure, an interesting conflation). Also notable: Theseus\u2019 opposition with Medea in the role of wicked step-mother (another possible glimmer of aristocratic youth in revolt against a female spiritual authority), Phaedra (Ariadne\u2019s sister and Theseus\u2019 wife who will later take on the role of Hippolytus\u2019 tormentor in that sacred tragedy), and Helen (who needs no introduction and whose Theseus abduction of is arguably the root cause of the Trojan War, also note her sister Clytemnestra).<br /> <br /> That was laying some foundations but let\u2019s really get into the meat now with Perseus. Somewhere in Graves, he puts forward the hypothesis that Perseus represents a certain class of aristocratic male youth of the archaic period (Who Frazer also characterized by their wanderings, their sudden rise to kingship after performance of heroic feats, their later mystified origins, etc.) who carry out a form of coup against older matriarchal religious systems. Perseus in particular gets pointed out for his role in the death of Medusa. As part of his wanderings he receives divine aid from Hermes &amp; Athena, both of whom are high ranking stooges of the Olympian sky-king. Hermes as his son and intelligencer (proficient as he is in roads, disguises, tricks, thievery, and deceit) and Athena as his self-begotten daughter and comprador in the mytho-historic defeat of the old feminine cults. They give Theseus the aid he requires to sneak up upon Medusa and the Gorgons unseen and slay them, which Graves identifies as a major point of usurpation of the customary religious rites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And we owe her a satire on the memory of the man who first tilted European Civilization off balance, by enthroning the restless and arbitrary male will under the name of Zeus and dethroning the female sense of orderliness, Themis. The Greeks knew him as Pterseus the Destroyer, the Gorgon-slaying warrior-prince from Asia, remote ancestor of the destroyers Alexander, Pompey &amp; Napoleon </div> </div> </div>The above is the prelude given by Robert Graves before his poem \u201cThe Destroyer\u201d, from somewhere in his Greek Myths. Sorry for not having the page number on hand, I\u2019m transcribing this from a screen shot.<br /> <br /> (As an aside: I\u2019m not going to defend the rigor of Frazer or Graves as historians of religion or Ancient Greece, but IMO their ideas are fitting for the romantic-influenced gothic-punk setting of the World of Darkness)<br /> <br /> Athena shows up again in the story of Bellerophon as the intercessor who grants him the golden bridle necessary to tame and master Pegasus. If we remember that Pegasus was born from the blood of Medusa landing upon Mother Earth (or erupting from the stump of her neck), this gift of a bridle, a classical symbol of superiority and domination, could be interpreted as another instance of Athena offering aid and assistance to that class of warrior-princes who would be the foot soldiers of religious insurrection against matrilineal custom (as she herself is, being born of father-alone). Notwithstanding that Bellerophon eventually oversteps his bounds and forces Zeus to reassert ultimate patriarchal authority, Bellerophon still accomplishes his purpose by slaying Chimera and mastering Perseus (however briefly). This added wrinkle in my opinion makes a lot of sense for the Black Furies\u2019 position in the setting.<br /> <br /> Plus, Athena appears as a major role in the final part of the Orestaia, wherein she oversees the trial of Orestes for matricide in Athens. Here Clytemnestra (Helen\u2019s sister btw, offering another connection to Theseus) has famously avenged the sacrifice of her daughter through the murder of Agamemnon (the proverbial king of kings in Homer) and is now being represented by the cthonic daemons the furies as Orestes\u2019 prosecutors. In opposition to them is that son of Zeus and lover of civilization, Apollo, serving as Orestes\u2019 defense. The trial takes on pretty strong undertones IMO of a Primordial/Cthonic/Feminine/\u201cSavage\u201d system of vengeance/justice which values mother-rite over father-rite and a Modern/Olympian/Masculine/\u201cCivilized\u201d system of vengeance/justice which values father-rite over mother-rite.<br /> <br /> Read this way we might even interpret Orestes as a sort of representative of the Minotaur. We first see the Minotaur represented as the victim of a usurpation against an old order, with hero slaying monster (depicted as Theseus overcoming the Minotaur with Ariadne\u2019s aid; although perhaps the Minotaur\u2019s subjection to Minos already represents a decay of a more pure BF mother-cult) and ends the cycle with the more ambiguous Orestes (of the generation after Perseus, Theseus, and the like) who instead of opposing a witch-sorceress or a monster is forced to conspire (with his sister Electra, in a role arguably analogous to Ariadne or Athena) against a purely mortal woman (the narrative of mother against son is sublimated in Theseus\u2019 struggle with his step-mother Medea but then fully embraced the following generation with Phaedra &amp; Hippolytus) [EDIT: actually scratch that, iirc Hippolytus is Theseus\u2019 son by the Amazon-queen Hippolyta, so that\u2019s still technically not incest; although Theseus &amp; Heracles subjugation of the Amazon-queens is also another interesting wrinkle to add to the Black Furies reason to loath these warrior-princes], and ends the second play/begins the third wandering the countryside like a beast and whether or not he\u2019s a civilized man or a lawless animal (in the eyes of the law/society) is not without question until the end of the third play.<br /> <br /> Perhaps somewhat tangential to the main thrust of this thread, but relevant enough as a possible lens for interpreting the Black Furies and the related stories that it felt worthwhile to include. Plus I do generally just find the idea to be a fascinating one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","user":"Gryffon15","date":". 12-13-2025, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T16:56:21-08:00","id":1556581,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that the Hunt Club from World of Darkness: Slashers (from the first edition of nWoD's Hunter the Vigil) might easily be retooled as a human Minotaur cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T19:41:47-08:00","id":1556588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556581#post1556581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me that the Hunt Club from World of Darkness: Slashers (from the first edition of nWoD's Hunter the Vigil) might easily be retooled as a human Minotaur cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh crap! That's actually a really good idea. I keep forgetting that CoD has some banger stuff.<br /> <br /> For how Minotaur's influence can manifest, what else can we propose here?<br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> mentioned, an aspect of d/evolution, where people think they're getting stronger in order to achieve some sort of goal (Kronik Fatigue from Hunter: the Parenting comes to mind). If this is more akin to a toxic mindset that obsesses over strength (which... if we're talking about the Wyrm, then that's just on par for the course), then that could also work.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/kJIOEQ7hAb4\" target=\"_blank\">Let's keep going.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28838,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28838-dafrontlinespecter","user":"DaFrontlineSpecter","date":". Chronicles having good material is why people cannibalize it TO THIS DAY! What was I thinking??? 12-13-2025, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28838-dafrontlinespecter","name":"DaFrontlineSpecter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T01:24:20-08:00","id":1556594,"title":"","content":"I like the ideas that the Minotaur myth may have started as a sun god or even a goddess, and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a>'s elaborations on how Minotaur may be, or at least have been, far more than it seems.<br /> <br /> From that, I actually think their grudge could come from a rather unexpected place: maybe Pegasus stole the aspects related to the sacred feminine from Minotaur.<br /> <br /> Minotaur may not have been originally so man-coded, or even a male at all, even if part or most of his current portfolio was already there. Maybe a more balanced spirit where natural strength and natural wisdom are two aspects of the same coin, maybe a proto-Artemis where instead of a hunter with a connection to beasts the goddess <i>is</i> beast and human. Maybe it happened because of Minotaur's corruption, or maybe it prompted the corruption, or just happened before it.<br /> <br /> Pegasus may even have stolen the followers themselves, the <b>Black Furies</b> from Minotaur, a very different Minotaur back then. In his eyes it's less about contempt for what Pegasus represent and more revolt against the usurper, and the Furies are seen as traitors even if they don't remember any of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T01:43:28-08:00","id":1556596,"title":"","content":"One more thing:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556562#post1556562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minotaur basically <i>knew </i><b>literally </b><u>every</u> Gift you can find - possibly even other Fera's gifts, plenty of overlaps already, and it not said he can't teach you this and that it just said... any gifts</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIR Gifts <b>are</b>, indeed, <i>gifts</i>. They're not something the spirits themselves know how to do (as spirits don't use them at all and frequently have no similar ability), but something the spirits grant as an extension of their nature.<br /> <br /> Garou can teach each other Gifts through a painstaking process, but that's so hard precisely because that's not how this is supposed to work. It's not a natural derivation of their nature and power like a Vampire's Disciplines, but the opposite, a small but significant change in their nature. What happens is that Shapeshifters are half spirit, and changing one's nature is something spirits <i>do</i>. But it isn't easy or simple, just possible, preferably through a process of ritual and symbolic exchanges that affects what a spirit (in this case the Garou) means, as meaning is the foundation of spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T07:13:17-08:00","id":1556605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556596#post1556596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AFAIR Gifts <b>are</b>, indeed, <i>gifts</i>. They're not something the spirits themselves know how to do (as spirits don't use them at all and frequently have no similar ability), but something the spirits grant as an extension of their nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>While this is true, Gifts reflect the facet represented by the spirit that grants/teaches it - eg. a spirit associated with war will not teach you Mother's Touch and a Shark Spirit will not teach you Monkey Tail - it is logical<br /> <br /> But the fact Minotaur was able to teach you any gift, means those gifts one shape or form reflected a facet of <i>him</i> - which is insane to think about how versatile he had to be to provide the gifts<br /> <br /> And if we move to the revised, toned down version of Minotaur, again we arrive to that curious situation where Minotaur <i>*knows* </i>what Spirit is able to teach what - something the spirits themselves and Theruges have problem to figure out - and point you to a spirit that <i>can</i> and <i>will do it</i> regardelss of their allegiance and the fact you are Minotraur's follower for some unfathomable reason again presenting that interesting setting where Minotaur have such knowledge and web of influence - either the Spirit owns him one, follows him, agree his agenda or simpyl afraid of him - all around the Umbra (umbras if you want to go an extra mile and looking for gifts tought by spirits of the Dark Umbra) to provide this &quot;favor&quot;<br /> <br /> Either way Minotaur had to be/has to be more than a brute he is commonly belived to be <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T17:25:30-08:00","id":1556679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556605#post1556605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the fact Minotaur was able to teach you any gift, means those gifts one shape or form reflected a facet of <i>him</i> - which is insane to think about how versatile he had to be to provide the gifts</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this was ever factually true. Unless I am unaware of some text you are referencing, I think you are misremembering some things.<br /> <br /> In the Outcasts sourcebook, Minotaur is mentioned as just one of several abandoned or ignored totems that the non-Sam Haight Skin Dancers have made contact with. Minotaur is specifically named, but the others are mentioned as &quot;others whose names I do not know&quot; by the in-character narrator. In other words, there are more such spirits. The narrator just knows the name of one of them. Furthermore, collectively they don't teach a whole lot of Gifts. The narrator explains &quot;a few minor gifts have been learned.&quot; This is a far cry from the statement that Minotaur can teach any gift or knows every gift. As written in Outcasts, the spirits who teach gifts to the Skin Dancers don't seem much different than any other spirits who teach gifts.<br /> <br /> The one thing that <i>is</i> different about the Skin Dancers learning Gifts is that they don't have rank (made explicit in Players Guide to Garou, but only assumed but not stated previously), but can learn gifts of higher rank. This is unusual because all other spirits only teach levels of Gift to Garou of appropriate rank, presumably because this is part of the Pact (not to mention done at appropriately ranked caerns (lest they offend the spirit), something mentioned in the corebooks in the Gifts section, but often overlooked by players and STs). Yet Minotaur and other inclined spirits seem willing to teach Gifts to the Skin Dancers despite not having rank (or being at appropriately ranked caerns).<br /> <br /> This places Minotaur and these other spirits (which I believe are best represented as his spirit brood) in a special category. It's like Minotaur is some kind of outcast or criminal spirit who operates outside the Pact either because he's some kind of &quot;criminal spirit&quot; acting in defiance of it, or perhaps it does not apply to him for whatever reason. I was planning on mentioning this in a future post, but wanted to mention it specifically here.<br /> <br /> I don't think that means Minotaur is a more powerful spirit, or that he is more potent in giftlore than other spirits. But he doesn't seem to abide by the pact. I think that's most likely because the writers simply forgot that there is a limitation within the game of when one learn's gifts. I doubt it was intentional. However, I do think it is appropriate and interesting that somehow Minotaur ignores the rules for whatever reason. It makes Minotaur seem more mysterious and even menacing as a rulebreaker. That adds to making a the faction more interesting as an antagonist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T17:36:40-08:00","id":1556680,"title":"","content":"I think the W20 corebook, in particular, has some things that are intriguing. It talks about Minotaur\u2019s spirit brood and its relation to Skin Dancers learning Gifts. In short, Minotaur\u2019s broods can teach about any Gift (at least up to level 3) even if for higher XP costs than even out-of-tribe/breed/auspice are for normal Garou. Presumably level 4 or 5 gifts are also available, but are far fewer in number (to be decided by the ST).<br /> <br /> So we know Minotaur has a spirit brood. Furthermore, this spirit brood is willing and able to teach Gifts despite Skin Dancers basically cheating the system. This not only has relevance for Skin Dancers, but I think it offers a source for Ronin to also learn new Gifts. Like Skin Dancers, normal Gaia spirits won\u2019t teach Gifts to Ronin. But if Minotaur\u2019s brood will teach Gifts to Dancers, why not Ronin as well? While Ronin are not supposed to be able learn Gifts and can\u2019t advance in Rank, the Skin Dancers don\u2019t have rank yet are able to learn not just Gifts, but Gifts higher than one level.<br /> <br /> Though obviously Skin Dancers have some patronage relationship with Minotaur, and Ronin do not, that does not mean Ronin can\u2019t petition Minotaur at all. The ST can allow Ronin to pack under Minotaur, and possibly even allow Ronin to learn Gifts without having Minotaur as a pack totem. They\u2019d just need to establish some good Chiminage with these spirits - perhaps honoring or worshipping Minotaur, donating Gnosis, agreeing to kill a child of Pegasus, or whatever it is the ST sees fit.<br /> <br /> This does not mean all Ronin would take advantage of it, but it\u2019s a way to not only allow some Ronin to learn new Gifts, but to build up Minotaur as an antagonist in the game. The Outcasts sourcebook teases that Ronin may be gathering at a mysterious \u201cCranberry Caern\u201d and that this may be a low level caern in New Jersey controlled by a pack of Skin Dancers.<br /> <br /> So this provides two options for us. The first is that some Ronin can still learn new Gifts from spirits provided they make deals with Minotaur. The second option is if some Ronin are flocking to Minotaur or even Skin Dancers to learn Gifts, then now Ronin can also become members of the &quot;new&quot; Skin Dancer tribe. This makes the Skin Dancers a lot more dangerous. Realistically, there are probably only so many kinfolk who can successfully become Garou through the Rite of Sacred Rebirth. The requirements are very steep. On the other hand, there's plenty of Ronin out there. And now they have the chance to be accepted as children of Minotaur as well. Indeed, they can probably become the majority of the tribe very quickly.<br /> <br /> Ronin learning Gifts is one thing. That won't substantially alter the setting. But allowing them to join the Skin Dancer tribe would probably be a big thing in any chronicle. I'm sure not all STs would want to allow this, but for those that do, it can be a way to generate a good crisis for the local Garou or even the Garou Nation as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T06:28:11-08:00","id":1556712,"title":"","content":"One thought that occurred to me on reading entries suggesting that there might be more to Minotaur than first appears is that Minotaur\u2019s charscter as \u2018The Beast In Man\u2019 logically suggests an element of the Jekyll and Hyde - it\u2019s quite possible that there are elements of both characterisations within this Spirit, but that the Players can never be quite certain whether they\u2019re going to get the Judge of the Underworld or the great grandfather of all supernatural Slasher villains (Which is, it should be said, a brilliant notion and kudos to the one who suggested it*).<br /> <br /> <br /> *Though it\u2019s amusing to note that Pasiphae\u2019s shame also confirms to the classic \u2018Huge, colourfully-murderous Bond villain henchman\u2019 archetype, part of my inspiration for seeing the legend of Theseus and the Minotaur as something of a Bronze Age Bond movie.<br /> <br /> <br /> It also occurs to me that whether or not Pegasus actually \u2018stole\u2019 the Black Furies from Minotaur, the latter might well believe this to be the case (Spirits are no less likely to remember the past as best suits their own self-image than any other thinking being): if nothing else, given that the Amazons famously went to war with Theseus, the Minotaur\u2019s killer, and assuming the Black Furies were near to the beating heart of any culture that inspired legends of the Amazons, it\u2019s possible the Tribe (or at least a camp within the Tribe) could well have had an association with Minotaur at one point.<br /> <br /> Given that war didn\u2019t go so very well for anyone, it\u2019s<br /> possible that Camp could gave been discredited and Minotaur\u2019s last chance to be a Totem spirit buried without a trace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T09:48:31-08:00","id":1556724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556679#post1556679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think this was ever factually true. Unless I am unaware of some text you are referencing, I think you are misremembering some things.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, checked it and yeah...<br /> Must be an older thing, like <i>Valkenburg Foundation</i> or Chaos Factor thing, or some LARP remnant<br /> I have learned long ago to doubt my own infallibility - so it is totally possible that particular detail is a localized Mandela Effect in my brain<br /> <br /> Still option B still valid and Minotaur must have an influence and extended knowledge of the spirits<br /> <br /> Speaking of spirits, in <b>20th Anniversary Edition</b> both <b>See Past the Skin</b> and <b>Mask Taint</b>\u200b Gifts states &quot;This Gift is taught by a servant of Minotaur&quot;<br /> So in WW20 he <i>have</i> servants<br /> <br /> (in earlier editions <b>See Past the Skin</b>\u200b was tought by a magpie-spirit and <b>Mask Taint</b>\u200b was taught by either a Puppeteer Bane or a corrupted chameleon-spirit, depending the edition - both actually opens an interesting situation, because the magpie-spirit not had to be corrupt, while a Puppeteer Bane - this enigmatic bad boy also gleefulyl teach the same Gift to Lords of the Summit, just a fun trivia - was... well... a Bane and the corrupted chameleon-spirit, was corrupted, yet both the pure magpie both the bane and the corrupted soirit was willing to teach the Skindancer follower of Minotaur)<br /> <br /> I wonder tho', what the Servant of Minotaur could be?<br /> Magpies still serve him?<br /> How Magpies - who teach Fools Gold and Thieving Talons of the Magpie (the Garou who learns this Gift becomes as gleeful a thief as the magpie, capable of stealing the magical abilities of others and using them herself. Any magical power can be stolen: a Gift used by another Garou, spirit Charms, a vampire's Disciplines, even a mage's spells - it is a Rank 5 tho' ) - ended up hanging around with Minotaur and the Skindancers...<br /> ...not to mention the Puppeteer Banes and corrupted chameleon-spirits<br /> Neither of them, well, Minotaur-like spirits - but again, no one said the servants have to be like the Boss","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-17T12:49:21-08:00","id":1556760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556724#post1556724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, checked it and yeah...<br /> Must be an older thing, like <i>Valkenburg Foundation</i> or Chaos Factor thing, or some LARP remnant<br /> I have learned long ago to doubt my own infallibility - so it is totally possible that particular detail is a localized Mandela Effect in my brain<br /> <br /> Still option B still valid and Minotaur must have an influence and extended knowledge of the spirits<br /> <br /> Speaking of spirits, in <b>20th Anniversary Edition</b> both <b>See Past the Skin</b> and <b>Mask Taint</b> Gifts states &quot;This Gift is taught by a servant of Minotaur&quot;<br /> So in WW20 he <i>have</i> servants<br /> <br /> (in earlier editions <b>See Past the Skin</b>\u200b was tought by a magpie-spirit and <b>Mask Taint</b>\u200b was taught by either a Puppeteer Bane or a corrupted chameleon-spirit, depending the edition - both actually opens an interesting situation, because the magpie-spirit not had to be corrupt, while a Puppeteer Bane - this enigmatic bad boy also gleefulyl teach the same Gift to Lords of the Summit, just a fun trivia - was... well... a Bane and the corrupted chameleon-spirit, was corrupted, yet both the pure magpie both the bane and the corrupted soirit was willing to teach the Skindancer follower of Minotaur)<br /> <br /> I wonder tho', what the Servant of Minotaur could be?<br /> Magpies still serve him?<br /> How Magpies - who teach Fools Gold and Thieving Talons of the Magpie (the Garou who learns this Gift becomes as gleeful a thief as the magpie, capable of stealing the magical abilities of others and using them herself. Any magical power can be stolen: a Gift used by another Garou, spirit Charms, a vampire's Disciplines, even a mage's spells - it is a Rank 5 tho' ) - ended up hanging around with Minotaur and the Skindancers...<br /> ...not to mention the Puppeteer Banes and corrupted chameleon-spirits<br /> Neither of them, well, Minotaur-like spirits - but again, no one said the servants have to be like the Boss</div> </div> </div> </div> Of course there\u2019s no guarantee the Magpies hang out with Minotaur because they like the cut of his job: it\u2019s possible they do so because he made them the metaphysical \u2018offer they can\u2019t refuse\u2019 (Though it\u2019s also possible Minotaur shows one face to them, another to his other servants).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-17T22:00:50-08:00","id":1556778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556724#post1556724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have learned long ago to doubt my own infallibility - so it is totally possible that particular detail is a localized Mandela Effect in my brain</div> </div> </div> </div>I often confuse my head canon with canon too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556724#post1556724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still option B still valid and Minotaur must have an influence and extended knowledge of the spirits</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I don't think this is so. Yeah, Minotaur's brood can teach most Gifts from level one to three, but that is not unusual. All Garou can learn all Gifts from level one to three. They just do it at much lower XP costs than Skin Dancers (3 xp per level for inside t/a/b or 5 xp for outside t/a/b, verus 6 xp for level for Skin Dancers). They can also learn all Gifts for level 4-5 Gifts, and Skin Dancers are more limited. Certainly an ST can decide to limit which outside t/a/b Gifts are available to Garou, but that applies to Skin Dancers as well.<br /> <br /> Rather than some amazing spirit influencer totem that has access to all sorts of Gifts, Minotaur is just a minor Incarna that is much more limited than any tribal totem. Of course, compared to many minor totems, he's building power and gathering spirits to his brood. I just don't think he's impressive compared to the standard tribal totems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556724#post1556724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in WW20 he <i>have</i> servants</div> </div> </div> </div>He definitely has a spirit brood. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556724#post1556724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder tho', what the Servant of Minotaur could be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say &quot;spirit of minotaur&quot; is another way of saying a spirit in his brood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556724#post1556724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magpies still serve him?</div> </div> </div> </div>I default to the Axis Mundi sourcebook as examples of what spirit broods are like. We have lots of examples of very similar spirits being in different broods (many variations of Raven spirits in many different broods, demonstrating that it is not unusual for the same type of spirit to be loyal to different totems). We also know there are many different reasons why spirits can choose to be part of a particular totem's brood. Some join to get the protection of said totem. Some join because the totem bullies/dominates them. Some join out of affinity.<br /> <br /> I imagine magpie spirits are likely divided between multiple spirit broods. Those that join Minotaur may do so because some spirits of cunning are drawn to his outcast nature, or because he bullies some into being part of his brood.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-17T22:06:54-08:00","id":1556779,"title":"","content":"Given the hidden history of Minoan Crete in the World of Darkness, I think it\u2019d be cool if there was some kind of unique occult secrets based on here. We have the fertility secrets of the Apis, the lore of the Toreador antediluvian (who given her masquerade of various love/war fertility goddesses with connections to sacred bulls might have a lot of connection to Apis associated societies), potential ties to the labyrinth of the Black Spiral, and the demonic rituals of the Baali. I\u2019m calling this group of lore as the <b>Cretan Mysteries</b>.<br /> <br /> Given the history, there probably is not any direct transmission of this lore to the modern day. However, I like the idea that ideas begun here crop up now and again in other books of occult lore from time to time, and that today there is some kind of reconstructed body of lore. How close to it is to the actual magical practices of WoD ancient Crete is irrelevant. Just that there are vestigal ties to the Minotaur Incarna that practitioners can use.<br /> <br /> I'm a big fan of using World of Darkness: Sorcerer in my chronicles. For those STs who do not possess that sourcebook, I usually recommend picking select Gifts to represent &quot;sorcery&quot;.<br /> <br /> Such sorcerers could be allies to the Skin Dancers, or entirely unrelated groups who may just interact with Minotaur, or develop devotion to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T01:41:03-08:00","id":1556782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556779#post1556779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the hidden history of Minoan Crete in the World of Darkness, I think it\u2019d be cool if there was some kind of unique occult secrets based on here. We have the fertility secrets of the Apis, the lore of the Toreador antediluvian (who given her masquerade of various love/war fertility goddesses with connections to sacred bulls might have a lot of connection to Apis associated societies), potential ties to the labyrinth of the Black Spiral, and the demonic rituals of the Baali. I\u2019m calling this group of lore as the <b>Cretan Mysteries</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <i>Enlightened Society of the Weeping Moon</i> from the <i>Wild West</i> supplements comes to mind. They were a masonic type sorcerous affiliation with a distorted view on Gaian lore - in part influenced by BSDs and/or the Tal'Mahe'Ra - and an internal structure that mimics the role of Garou Auspices. The society dissolved shortly before the first World War.<br /> <br /> I think they would make a good predecessor organization for a modern Cretan Mysteries society and could act as a structural template. Their 'Theurges', called Horned Moons, practice a form of spirit control that is vaguely based on Saturnalia. Probably not a big stretch to assume they may also develop a shapeshifting path based on Lupercalia that ties them to the Skin Dancers and fertility Rites.<br /> <br /> Diaspora of the Weeping Moon could have picked up on lore from an older Cretan society and fused their own into it to make up something new. I think they are pretty compatible with the mix of influences.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T11:24:21-08:00","id":1556799,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s amusing to imagine Academic arguments between ex-Moon luminaries as they try to remember which bits of the \u2018Minoan Rite\u2019 were tradition, which supposition and which mere invention some years after the inception (\u201cRevitalisation!\u201d) of this particular occult rite - it being very, very important to keep track of this sort of thing when actual Occult Entities are involved, just in case somebody crosses an \u2018i\u2019 or dots a \u2018T\u2019. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-19T12:19:25-08:00","id":1556840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556782#post1556782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diaspora of the Weeping Moon could have picked up on lore from an older Cretan society and fused their own into it to make up something new. I think they are pretty compatible with the mix of influences.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I am aware of the Enlightened Society of the Weeping Moon, I don't have any Wild West sourcebooks and don't know much about them or how they were used in game as antagonists. However, I agree that groups like this would be a good place to name drop some references to the Cretan Mysteries and minotaur.<br /> <br /> In the back story of Samuel Haight, we're told that he learned Thaumaturgy and lore about &quot;powers even a mere Kinfolk could learn&quot; from a Tremere warlock's library (whom he had destroyed). So references of this could be known to the Tremere, or at least certain secret societies or individual chantries as the ST wishes.<br /> <br /> Haight then travelled around the world learning lots of different occult secrets before learning the Rite of Sacred Rebirth from a cult in India. That perhaps might be a bit far to learn anything that originated in Crete, but it's not impossible. Or it might be an indication that perhaps the Minotaur spirit was more active around the world than was suspected. Of course, we don't have a direct connection between Minotaur and that Rite. That rite came first, and the Skin Dancers contact with Minotaur came later. Yet personally I would lean towards some real connection between the Rite of Sacred Rebirth and Minotaur.<br /> <br /> References to Minotaur or spirit entities that might be Minotaur would be a good way to build up suspense. Moloch isn't described as a bull in the Bible, but it's a popular image to depict Moloch as a bull headed idol. And there are lots of other references to sacred bulls in world mythology that either refer to the Minotaur spirit, or which this spirit might masquerade as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-19T13:44:29-08:00","id":1556842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556840#post1556840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, we don't have a direct connection between Minotaur and that Rite.</div> </div> </div> </div>In The Apocalyptic Record, a Glass Walker Kinfolk, Dr. Alia Chukwuka's research notices the connection between the Skin-Dancers and their totem Minotaur. In that the Rite of Sacred Rebirth seems to be a corrupted version of the Gumagan Rite, Rite of Spirit-Skin-Blessing. She concludes that the vengeful spirit of the last Apis - filled with hatred and seeking revenge upon its Black Fury tormentors and Pegasus - would know how to create such a rite due to the Apis' role as matchmakers<br /> <br /> To give the whole thing a twist, according Shattered Dreams, the Ritual of Sacred Rebirth was first developed by Aztec Kinfolk of the Balam in Mexico.<br /> While what is in Shattered Dreams is usually <i>non-canonical</i> it is still an interesting little lore piece - Princess Ichtaca driven by jealousy and resentment edicated her life to discovering a ritual or magic that would give her the same abilities as her brothers and father. Risking her life and sanity, she made pacts with strange entities she barely understood<br /> Now who was the residente of Crete, the fabled hometown of Minotaur, who later ended up in the other side of the planet and became the War god of the Aztecs...?<br /> Nergal/ <b>Huitzilopochtli </b>(who himself claimed that he had a hand in the development of the Olmecs and following civilizations since 1200 BC - it actually fits the Baali time line and how the second Baali war only ended when Sutekh personally arrived and with his childer, through sorcery, triggered the eruption of a volcano on the nearby island of Thera, which devastated much of Crete)<br /> The same Nergal/ <b>Huitzilopochtli </b>\u200bwho later had a run in with Samuel<br /> <br /> It is just another fun little detail<br /> And while no definite mention of the Baali in India the Black Death is widely believed to have originated in Central Asia and spread via trade routes, including paths through India - where Samuel learned the rite from a cult - to Europe and &quot;Namtaru&quot;, Nergal's sugardady was called the Spreader of Plagues... while Nergal travelled to the west, I can easly see some of his brood fled to the opposite direction<br /> <br /> So Nergal in that quasi-cannonical scenario could be the one who taught the Princes the version of the Rite - or put her in contact with Minotaur, who he may or may not knew perhaps personally<br /> If you want to stretch the whole thing, you can add when Nergal took over Crete he accidentally (or purposefully) released/freed Minotaur from &quot;the Black Fury tormentors and Pegasus&quot; in one way or another, either by corrupting the local girls who &quot;tormented&quot; Minotaur or simply just killed them - interastingly in that scenario Minotaur wouldn't be the only &quot;heavy hitter&quot; captive of the Black Furies. Non less than <i>three</i> Tallons of the Wyrm were imprisoned and kept in their caerns; one was imprisoned at the Black Fury caern, the Sept of Artemis, on in the Caern, Sept of the Black Pegasus and the third, Thrassus, the Smallest Finger aka. &quot;Exhibit 338&quot;, was sealed beneath the Sept of Bygone Visions in the Mediterranean, a caern under control of the Black Furies. \u200b<br /> <br /> It is of course a headcanon and just connection a few throw away mentions, but still a fun thought exercise<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-22T10:48:48-08:00","id":1556919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556842#post1556842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To give the whole thing a twist, according Shattered Dreams, the Ritual of Sacred Rebirth was first developed by Aztec Kinfolk of the Balam in Mexico.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't know this was a thing canonically. I was going to do a post on how other Changing Breeds might also have Skin Dancer versions, and now it turns out someone else already did this.<br /> <br /> I think it's a great idea, and it is interesting to ponder that the &quot;Skin Dancer&quot; tribe under Minotaur might not just be a Garou tribe, but a collection of multiple faux-Changing Breeds. It would be a perverse union of the Changing Breeds under Minotaur that the actual Gaian Changing Breeds have trouble doing.<br /> <br /> I would personally limit such breeds to be big predator animals in order to emphasize the &quot;beast within man&quot; aspect, but other STs may prefer any and all breeds to be potential victims of the Rite of Sacred Rebirth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556842#post1556842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now who was the residente of Crete, the fabled hometown of Minotaur, who later ended up in the other side of the planet and became the War god of the Aztecs...?<br /> Nergal/ <b>Huitzilopochtli </b>(who himself claimed that he had a hand in the development of the Olmecs and following civilizations since 1200 BC - it actually fits the Baali time line and how the second Baali war only ended when Sutekh personally arrived and with his childer, through sorcery, triggered the eruption of a volcano on the nearby island of Thera, which devastated much of Crete)<br /> The same Nergal/ <b>Huitzilopochtli </b>\u200bwho later had a run in with Samuel</div> </div> </div> </div>It's interesting if we want to use this Apocalyptic Record and Shattered Dreams version, as involving Crete, the Gumagan (who are found only in Australiasia and Melanesia), India (where Sam Haight learned it) and Mesoamerica means the presence of Minotaur and some version of this rite has wide ranging roots.<br /> <br /> I like the ties you speculate between the Baali in Crete and Mesoamerica with this rite because it does fit canon. I wonder how exactly a corrupted rite of the Gumagan made its way to the Baali originally. While it's not impossible for a Baali to perhaps find their way to them, the text implies the rite originated there and somehow made their way to the Baali in Crete instead. I supposed it'd have to be that somehow that corrupted rite was transmitted to the Mokole-mbembe of the Nile, as knowledge of it there could be transmitted to Minoan Crete.<br /> <br /> In this version, the Baali were perhaps not the inventor of the Rite of Sacred Rebirth, but could have acted as a means of transmission of the rite and the &quot;minotaur cult&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-23T11:29:06-08:00","id":1556937,"title":"","content":"Given that Alexander the Great and his Successors carried Hellenistic culture as far as the Hindu Kush (I believe there was even an Alexandrian successor state that synthesised Greek &amp; Hindu culture to some degree in that region) it would not have been impossible for a Minoan rite to have been carried as far east as India, assuming that a Hellenistic culture was the intermediary.<br /> <br /> Heck, given that the Ancient Greeks were at least aware of the existence of India (and that trade routes between India and the Mediterranean have existed since the time of Ancient Egypt) it\u2019s at least somewhat possible that a refugee from Crete with their share of Minoan secrets could well have chosen India as a refuge, thinking it safely-distant from home and so very large as to be quite easy to find a hiding place in (Especially by the standards of Crete and the Greek homeland).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-25T17:56:23-08:00","id":1556999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556937#post1556937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Given that Alexander the Great and his Successors carried Hellenistic culture as far as the Hindu Kush (I believe there was even an Alexandrian successor state that synthesised Greek &amp; Hindu culture to some degree in that region) it would not have been impossible for a Minoan rite to have been carried as far east as India, assuming that a Hellenistic culture was the intermediary.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not necessary for the Baali to wait until Alexander's invasions, but it does provide a great pretext and is a natural way to explain it. Also, just because the Baali were involved in Crete and lead to the general corruption there, it does not mean the transmitter of the Rite of Sacred Rebirth was a Baali. Once a cult is established, Greek mortal (renegade kinfolk of any Changing Breed) practitioners could have been the ones who followed in the wake of Alexander's invasions. Since I like tying the Baali to Crete, but not maing them participants in this cult/faction itself, I'll be going with the latter idea in my chronicles.<br /> <br /> Since the Asiatic lion had an original range from Greece to India (not to mention North Africa), I like the idea maybe it was renegade Simba kinfolk who originally expanded the knowledge.<br /> <br /> I'm still trying to figure out how a corrupted Gumagan rite could have been involved. And I would have that question even if the issue of Crete never came up. The isolation of Australasia simply makes it hard to explain how it got to Eurasia at all. However, Mnesis, various Mokole Gifts and Rites, and the tradition of &quot;wanderers&quot; who travel to pass on Gaia's memories to others can also easily justify the passing of knowledge that later got discovered and corrupted, so I'm not too worried about it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-25T18:15:03-08:00","id":1557000,"title":"","content":"Another thing to do is lean heavily into the idea that this is a kinfolk secret society. There's lots of reason why kinfolk (and not just those of Garou) may resent or be envious of their Changing Breed. They are immune to the Delirium, have knowledge of their society and customs, and are capable of possessing some (limited) supernatural powers of their own. And since they do reproduce their Changing Breeds, there's not much to prevent a corrupt colony of kinfolk to sacrifice their own children in order to harvest skins to be used later. That's obviously twisted, gruesome and horrific, but that is what would make it an interesting antagonist in a chronicle. The PCs find a &quot;lost&quot; community of isolated kinfolk, and they initially think it's a great find - until they realize this village are Skin Dancer kinfolk who have been harvesting pelts for a long time, and their isolation was on purpose, and they see the PCs as a threat for exposing them. Maybe it's a community founded by renegades of multiple Breeds.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk can learn Gifts. Even though spirits are unlikely to teach a lot of Gifts to kinfolk, once one is taught, that kinfolk does have the option of teaching others that same Gift just like Garou can. That means a kinfolk community of Skin Dancers can pass on these Gifts to each other in perpetuity, slowly building knowledge of new Gifts throughout the centuries whenever one of them somehow picks it up. Of course, the entire kinfolk community does not need to know these, just a select group of elders and &quot;wise&quot; people.<br /> <br /> You can combine this with some of these kinfolk also knowing one or more Paths of Sorcery that they also pass on to each other. Then maybe even Numina like the Soulstealing in Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes.<br /> <br /> It's one thing to fight a small pack of Skin Dancers. Another to fight an entire small community of kinfolk who've been following corrupt ways for years, decades, or perhaps even centuries, and have their own sick Litany and mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-26T02:16:03-08:00","id":1557005,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556999#post1556999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still trying to figure out how a corrupted Gumagan rite could have been involved.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is bit of a headache I must admit, but I came up with a few &quot;solutions&quot;<br /> The first is the obvious what you mentioned, the &quot;wanderers&quot; , there are indeed Mokol\u00e9 whos job is basically to keep the Memory &quot;fresh&quot; and expand the Mnesis by mating or with rite &quot;<b>Last Communion</b>&quot; saving the mnesis one of the dying or with the <b>Bowl of Mnesis</b> Fetish or just &quot;copy&quot; the mensis<br /> Or simply discover it via a Mnesis quest<br /> Then from pont A to point B to C, untill it ended up currupted in thr wrong hands<br /> <br /> Following the Baali idea, they have it easy, Demons of any kind from the Fallen (Demon: the Fallen actually have throwaway lines of Spirits and Spirit world and a few hints, - if you go with Revelations of the Dark Mother, this world/civilisation is not the first) to lovecraftian entities, True Fae, Secret Masters, whatever are the Outer Things the Yama Queen Tou Mu found and of course whatever you want to call a Demon easly could simply gave them the knowledge - or at least the Kinfolk they corrupted<br /> Would you sell your soul to become a Shapeshifter son? Cool! Sign here. A bit of a monekey paw deal, I never said I will transform you personally, but here is a neat little rite you can use... sure it requires a few &quot;things&quot; but grab a skinning knife, this will be hell of a ride!<br /> <br /> Another solution came with suprisingly from the Mage side.<br /> The <b>Muvians</b><br /> During their reign, they established a worldwide network of colonies built around Nodes, including one in what is today Alice Springs, Australia. - are an extinct species of sapient, tool-using humanoid reptiles native to the prehistoric Pacific supercontinent of Mu.<br /> But they may not that dead after all...<br /> <b>Urr Re'ok</b>\u200b was a member of a prehistoric saurian humanoid species (not explicitly stated to be a Muvian) allegedly capable of True Magic. She resembled a pink, humanoid protoceratops and spend her life on the Etherite space station located in the Moon's Penumbra, the <b>Victoria Station</b>\u200b - the Avatar Storm offed her probably, but still, while she was not 100% a Muvian who in turm may or may not be Mokol\u00e9, it is a nice possibility<br /> What the Gumagan had was already a remnant/memory of something older and since it they had a worldwide network? Either on Crate or India could had ruins and artifacts (and even a few spirits lingering around) the Baali or anyone lese who were curious enough to discover<br /> <br /> Speaking of possibilites, Shattered Dreams introduced the <b>Defiler Kings</b>, a small group of survivors of the Lizard Kings who turned to the Wyrm and became the first Mnetics, who can warp the spiritual landscape of any Realm to their liking given time, drawing upon their understanding of the &quot;old Mnesis&quot;<br /> And of course the <b>Mnetics</b> themselves, the Eaters of Secrets the Fallen Mokol\u00e9 from W20 Book of the Wyrm<br /> Both group is famous for stelaing memories, and more importantly changing and corrupting them<br /> And neither have a love for the Changing Breeds or the modern world\u200b - this regard corrupting the memory of a sacred Rite and spreading it to turn the &quot;world order&quot; upside down by giving the bitter Kinfolks a way to become Shifters themselves seems logical - I mean the Kinfolks outnumber the shapeshifters lets say even if 10 to 1 that is a huge one, and it is a delightful twist to let the the Breeds become destroyed from within, possibly replaced by something that at the end of the day, owes you a big one - or could be molded<br /> <br /> So as you said, there are pelnty of way to explain how and why that Rite is around\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T10:37:20-08:00","id":1557097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1556999#post1556999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not necessary for the Baali to wait until Alexander's invasions, but it does provide a great pretext and is a natural way to explain it. Also, just because the Baali were involved in Crete and lead to the general corruption there, it does not mean the transmitter of the Rite of Sacred Rebirth was a Baali. Once a cult is established, Greek mortal (renegade kinfolk of any Changing Breed) practitioners could have been the ones who followed in the wake of Alexander's invasions. Since I like tying the Baali to Crete, but not maing them participants in this cult/faction itself, I'll be going with the latter idea in my chronicles.<br /> <br /> Since the Asiatic lion had an original range from Greece to India (not to mention North Africa), I like the idea maybe it was renegade Simba kinfolk who originally expanded the knowledge.<br /> <br /> I'm still trying to figure out how a corrupted Gumagan rite could have been involved. And I would have that question even if the issue of Crete never came up. The isolation of Australasia simply makes it hard to explain how it got to Eurasia at all. However, Mnesis, various Mokole Gifts and Rites, and the tradition of &quot;wanderers&quot; who travel to pass on Gaia's memories to others can also easily justify the passing of knowledge that later got discovered and corrupted, so I'm not too worried about it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> In this context it\u2019s also worth noting that Cretan archers were amongst the most keenly-sought and far-travelled mercenaries in the Eastern Mediterranean even before the Age of Alexander.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding the Rite itself, is it possible for such a thing to be conjured up through a process of convergent evolution? (That is, different populations arriving at much the same solution to the same - or similar - challenges after separate processes of development).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T10:39:42-08:00","id":1557098,"title":"","content":"Also, Holy Moley, that hidden kinfolk cult village sounds like exactly the sort of nasty business the Shadow Lords were born and made to handle: so help me, those Skindancers might even deserve to have Grandfather Thunder\u2019s children rain down on him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T15:29:12-08:00","id":1557110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557097#post1557097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Rite itself, is it possible for such a thing to be conjured up through a process of convergent evolution? (That is, different populations arriving at much the same solution to the same - or similar - challenges after separate processes of development).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's all sorts of ways you can justify creating the Rite of Sacred Rebirth. You don't even need it to be based on that supposed Gumagan Rite. I'm just talking about it in case someone wants to utilize that bit of lore. Before that bit came up, I just said that Minoan Crete is where that rite was first created, and I could keep using that in my own chronicles.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T15:47:34-08:00","id":1557112,"title":"","content":"So I finally get to the idea that was actually the prompt to create this thread in the first place. I while ago I came across <a href=\"https://rogues-repast.blogspot.com/2019/05/harry-clarke-bestiary-project-bull-witch.html\" target=\"_blank\">this webpage about a D&amp;D monster based on an artwork from the classical illustrator Harry Clarke</a>.<br /> <br /> I immediately thought this monster, the Bull Witch, would be great to reinterpret for the World of Darkness for Minotaur. It involves bulls, a desire for animalistic/masculine strength, and the corruption of a maiden fits a spirit that hates Pegasus.<br /> <br /> I thought it would make a great fomori that utilizes another corrupted version of the rite. Just add fomori powers like Bestial Mutation and other powers with that form (Armored Hide, Derserker, Claws and Fang (to simulate the horns), Unnatural Strength). Plus any others the ST thinks appropriate.<br /> <br /> As part of Minotaur\u2019s feud with Pegasus, Minotaur seeks to pervert the sacred feminine that Pegasus protects. The Bull Witch is Minotaur\u2019s corrupt and mocking version of the Apis. These spirits retain distant memories when the aurochs ran wild and free, and know the secrets of the Apis. They seek revenge against the Garou and mankind for taming and breaking the spirits of the bulls\u2019 wild ancestors.<br /> <br /> Such an encounter with a coven of Bull Witches probably won't mean much on its own, but for a chronicle that deals with the threat of Minotaur, it would make a good encounter that builds up its menace as the PCs learn about other ways that the Minotaur spirit is affecting the world. It can be a way to learn of the Cretan Mysteries, possible connections with other groups affiliated with Minotaur and more.<br /> <br /> And of course, perhaps there are more such groups based on other powerful animals - perhaps all of them seemingly tied to animals connected to the extinct Lost Changing Breeds. There's different ways you can go with this.<br /> <br /> Since these would be fomori, it probably makes Minotaur more Wyrm corrupted that some might like.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-08T15:08:26-08:00","id":1557387,"title":"","content":"Looks like this topic may have exhausted itself. But before I abandon it completely, I want to revisit the two possible Skin Dancer caerns mentioned back in Outcasts. Since this information is (mostly) provided IC, there's also mention of doubts whether it is true. I consider these weasel words as just allowing STs to determine the actual factual status in their own chronicles so they don't have to care about players saying one way or another what is canon.<br /> <br /> The first is the Dutchman's Caern in Arizona located at the Superstition Mountains. For those that don't know, this is just east the Phoenix metro area. It's very close to Phoenix. It's a powerful rank 4 caern (Enigmas and Wisdom) that is a lost Nuwisha caern with the totem of &quot;Trickster.&quot; An image of Sam Haight himself supposedly revealed itself and led them to the caern. If you want to include this in your chronicle, this is a fairly powerful caern and should be a stronghold of the Skin Dancers, helped by ancient magics hiding the place. It also opens up the possibility that Nuwisha may or may not also be involved. If so, I doubt very much this is intended to be a stronghold of the Wyrm aligned Skin Dancers, and may be a plot of Trickster to align them to Gaia. If the ST wants to keep them more villainous, I'd probably ditch the Nuwisha angle and possibly change the totem to something else.<br /> <br /> The second is the Cranberry Caern in the pinewoods of New Jersey. This is a weak rank 1 caern (Stamina) with totem of Magpie. The hook here is that this is the caern that Ronin may be gathering at in order to ally with the Skin Dancers or possibly even join them. The sourcebook states that &quot;all four factions&quot; of the post-Haight Skin Dancers are involved here. However, a Rank 1 caern is just not going to have many packs or Garou present. I think the canon guidelines is up to 10, so this may just mean 1 or 2 packs with their members divided on what to do. While it says the Skin Dancers don't let the Garou know they are Skin Dancers, the only reason I can think of why Skin Dancers would tolerate or even encourage Ronin to attend their caerns would be to try to recruit them into the tribe.<br /> <br /> So they're fairly basic, but I think they do a good job of presenting options for the ST. In both cases, it would be very easy to move the locations of the caerns or adjust other details about them to better fit whatever the ST wants. As a sourcebook, Outcasts put its weight behind the idea of Skin Dancers as a playable (non-Wyrm aligned) faction like Ronin. Its caern descriptions fit that. If you want them to be more as antagonists and villains though, you wouldn't need to work too hard to depict them differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T02:38:05-08:00","id":1557410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf#post1556500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As people know, Minotaur is the Incarna patron of the Skin Dancers. Although the Skin Dancers were introduced earlier, I believe the first mention of Minotaur himself is from 1995\u2019s Outcasts sourcebook where he is given the epitaph <i>That-Which-Howls-In-The-Forests</i>. He\u2019s since been developed a little bit more in Players Guide to Garou and some of the W20 material.<br /> <br /> I think Minotaur has potential to become something more than just the patron of the Skin Dancers. Note that when I describe this as a faction, I don\u2019t mean the Minotaur Incarna is leading or controlling some kind of conspiracy or army. Just that Minotaur can be the source of additional antagonists than just the Skin Dancers, and that these different groups may or may not cooperate with each other locally.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll be using this thread to explore some ideas I\u2019ve been having. More to come.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I've heard, Minotaur's status is being threatened by Tick, who is trying to usurp his patronage over the Skin Dancers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Since Minotaur is supposed to represent casting aside your humanity to become a savage beast, I could see Pentex acquiring him for their Mockery Breeds program.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T13:10:09-08:00","id":1557427,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, firstly that \u2018Bull Witch\u2019 was a great pick - ahe definitely has a superbly folkloric feel; secondly, the notion of the Wyrm finally getting bitten by something very like one if it\u2019s very own \u201cAt last we have found a precious treasure to cheri- WHOOPS, we have been possessed by the lingering power of an immense cosmic entity\u201d gambits brings a smile to my face in a very Nuwisha style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T11:32:06-08:00","id":1557551,"title":"","content":"Upon further introspect, I could see an argument made for a redeemed Minotaur becoming a totem of the Red Talons, and specifically offering patronage to those of the Homid born that were recently allowed to join the tribe's ranks in W5.<br /> <br /> Basically calling out to those who grew disillusioned with Humanity, and seek to adopt a simpler, more animalistic lifestyle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T22:57:53-08:00","id":1557577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557410#post1557410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've heard, Minotaur's status is being threatened by Tick, who is trying to usurp his patronage over the Skin Dancers.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the W20 adventure sourcebook The Skinner, Tick is a pack totem of the NPC Skin Dancer pack, and it is trying to usurp Minotaur's status as leader of the Skin Dancers. I'd make the Tick Incarna part of Minotaur's spirit brood. I'm not a particular fan of that sourcebook, but I'll pick whatever I can use from it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557410#post1557410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Minotaur is supposed to represent casting aside your humanity to become a savage beast, I could see Pentex acquiring him for their Mockery Breeds program.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that Minotaur would be a good pick pick for a patron of fomori Mockery Breeds, but that is now how they decided to go with it. The sourcebooks have always put Minotaur in the position of being Wyrm tainted but not really of the Wyrm. Many authors don't know if they want the Skin Dancers to be antagonists or possible allies. I think it's best if that is left to individual STs to decide based on the needs of their chronicles. I'm inclined to make Minotaur more of an antagonist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T00:01:05-08:00","id":1557578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557577#post1557577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many authors don't know if they want the Skin Dancers to be antagonists or possible allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Garou was <i>always</i> a dying race - either Naturally (simply they die to fast to replenish the numbers; one might say natural selection. And face it Nature was never a kindly one &quot;Green mother Nature, Red of tooth and claw.&quot;) or either because Gaia (made them to be soldiers who technically failed and defiled their duties so Gaia either decided okay, enough is enough an no more Garou will born and will make new defenders - like she did with the Kitsune - or either because the Apocalypse no more cub will born so they could prepare for the Big Battle)<br /> <br /> Whatever the case, in every edition the Garou as a race was always danced on the edge of extinction<br /> While the Black Spiral Dancers?<br /> Well smiliarly but they not really had problem to breed Metis and that - and the fact they &quot;recrutied&quot; from other Tribes - a bit balanced out. Not just balance out, but they, according official soruces was the only tribe increasing in population, possibly making up a <b><i>tenth</i></b> of all werewolves, dwarfing other tribes<br /> <br /> That is kind of huge<br /> <br /> The Ritual of Sacred Rebirth had a wee bit of &quot;drawback&quot; - the Kinfolk must slay five different Garou, all within the same lunar auspice, and completed within that same auspice as well, skin them and with the pelts of five Garou induce the First Change in a Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> And since this is World of <b>Darkness </b>- and the Garou are more than desperate it was always suprising the whole deal not took a really dark turn where the Garou decided okay, lets hunt and breed Black Spiral Dancers for ritualistic purposes<br /> I mean the ritual only say, you have to kill and skin a Garou for their pelt and setting up a Black Spiral Dancer Metis breeding program?<br /> You don't even have to wait that long, Metis born with pelts...<br /> <br /> Very twisted, very dark, and had a very dystopian chronicle where my players faced the moral choice not unlike in Soylent Green discovering what was the price to refill the Garou Grand Army's numbers to keep Gaia safe...<br /> <br /> But even if you don't go global, Garou tend to have &quot;bright ideas&quot; (the CyberWolf project, the cloning of the Bunyip... just name a few)<br /> Or the Pentex discover the Rite and decide, okay the Black Spiral Dancers are too insane, too dangerous... but we could use them to make our own Garou out of sane and indocrinated kinfolks...<br /> <br /> Just a few dark ideas to spice things up<br /> <br /> (And the Danislav are the good example, Spirits not always look down such a bright ideas)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 01-14-2026, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T05:13:59-08:00","id":1557590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557577#post1557577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sourcebooks have always put Minotaur in the position of being Wyrm tainted but not really of the Wyrm. Many authors don't know if they want the Skin Dancers to be antagonists or possible allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I confess I know little on the specifics of Skinwalkers, but what I do know about them is that they are portrayed as being super EVIL. Like, demonic in how they go about terrorizing people.<br /> <br /> If the Skindancers are supposed to represent them in Apocalypse, then they should be antagonists.<br /> <br /> Skinwalkers also existed in Changeling as one of the Thallain, gaining the ability to shapeshift into animals by eating pieces of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T05:18:25-08:00","id":1557591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557578#post1557578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Garou was <i>always</i> a dying race - either Naturally (simply they die to fast to replenish the numbers; one might say natural selection. And face it Nature was never a kindly one &quot;Green mother Nature, Red of tooth and claw.&quot;) or either because Gaia (made them to be soldiers who technically failed and defiled their duties so Gaia either decided okay, enough is enough an no more Garou will born and will make new defenders - like she did with the Kitsune - or either because the Apocalypse no more cub will born so they could prepare for the Big Battle)</div> </div> </div> </div>Kitsune are even worse on the repopulation issue, for two very major reasons:<br /> <br /> 1 - They can not increase their numbers outside of Asia. Children born in different regions will never undergo the First Change.<br /> <br /> 2 - At least one of their parents will always die at the moment of their birth. Meaning that for every Kitsune they gain, they lose one in the process.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557578#post1557578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Ritual of Sacred Rebirth had a wee bit of &quot;drawback&quot; - the Kinfolk must slay five different Garou, all within the same lunar auspice, and completed within that same auspice as well, skin them and with the pelts of five Garou induce the First Change in a Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> And since this is World of <b>Darkness </b>- and the Garou are more than desperate it was always suprising the whole deal not took a really dark turn where the Garou decided okay, lets hunt and breed Black Spiral Dancers for ritualistic purposes<br /> I mean the ritual only say, you have to kill and skin a Garou for their pelt and setting up a Black Spiral Dancer Metis breeding program?<br /> You don't even have to wait that long, Metis born with pelts...</div> </div> </div> </div>The ritual also says that if the pelts are not given willingly, the ritual results in you becoming wyrm tainted.<br /> <br /> Somehow, I don't see BSD prisoners allowing themselves to be skinned in the service of Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 01-14-2026, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T06:14:22-08:00","id":1557595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557591#post1557591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The ritual also says that if the pelts are not given willingly, the ritual results in you becoming wyrm tainted.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes<br /> But not state <i>how</i> deeply<br /> Tainted like a Garou who descended with his pack in a Pit, slaughtered a dozen of Banes and Fomori, went toe-to-toe with a pack of Black Spiral Dancers, and thanks to the spiritual polution and gifts, talens and fetishes ended up reeking of Wyrm<br /> Or<br /> &quot;Inherently&quot; tainted like lets say a BSD <br /> <br /> A Rite of Clensing is enough or you need a trip to Erebus to get rid of the Taint<br /> <br /> How deeply that Taint effects you?<br /> <br /> Not to mention a little taint in a broken diying wolrd is not a huge price to pay - heck the Lords even have a Gift to hide it<br /> <br /> Or these new kind of Skindancers could adapt a Howl of the Devil Tiger Dharma-mindset - I became a Holy Monster of Gaia to save her...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T06:25:36-08:00","id":1557596,"title":"","content":"I think becoming a serial killer in the quest to cast aside your humanity and transform into a literally rage fueled berserker qualifies as pretty deeply tainted. Especially if you're planning to create a farm of incestuous mutants for the soul purpose of mass producing the ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T06:28:24-08:00","id":1557597,"title":"","content":"I think you completly missed the point why and what I wrote, but okay","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T06:30:36-08:00","id":1557598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557597#post1557597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you completly missed the point why and what I wrote, but okay</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I got the point.<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly, the Galliard Group said that you start off with 1 point of Wyrm Taint if the pelts are collected unwillingly. Also, the Garou will pretty much try to slaughter you on sight if they find out you did this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T11:48:30-08:00","id":1557608,"title":"","content":"Also, that\u2019s just the <i>Gaian</i> Garou: imagine what the Black Spiral Dancers will do to you if they get wind of this particularly horrible practice being applied to <i>their</i> relatives.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Also, and this is only tangentially-related, but I\u2019d like to point out that the Black Spiral Dancers are making themselves the largest single tribe only in the short term by breeding Metis en mass: this isn\u2019t a sustainable policy applied over the long-term, this is a \u2018No Tomorrow! APOCALYPSE NOW!\u2019 policy which will only fail to come back and bite them if the Last Battle happens sooner rather than later - which means that \u2018farming\u2019 Black Spiral Dancers will not only be far more difficult on a practical level than you make it sound, it\u2019s also wasting time you could be applying to more important battles and labours*).<br /> <br /> <br /> *In addition to being out and out monstrous morally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T14:49:22-08:00","id":1557619,"title":"","content":"Even if the idea is that Garou teach the Rite of Sacred Rebirth to kinfolk for the purposes of hunting Black Spiral Dancers and enabling them to become Garou, the big problem with that strategy is that you let the cat out of the bag. There is nothing to stop those kinfolk from turning on you. As a general idea, this is just bad.<br /> <br /> However, there's plenty of evidence of Garou being stupid and some Garou willing to deal with Wyrm minions for the purposes of fighting the greater evil. As such, I do think there's sufficient evidence to justify an ST for using this as a plot element in their chronicle if they wish.<br /> <br /> A pack of Shadow Lords of the Bringers of Light camp decide to help a select group of kinfolk become Garou and eliminate a Hive of Black Spiral Dancers. Just one more &quot;triumph&quot; of them using the Wyrm's methods but overcoming the corruption themselves! Or perhaps its Silent Striders of the Eaters of the Dead camp. Or perhaps its the Society of Bitter Frost among the Uktena. Or desperate Bone Gnawers from a sept that already tolerates Man Eaters and the like. Or whatever group of dubious Garou the ST wishes.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps instead of targeting BSDs alone, they target Ronin as well or perhaps lone Metis. Anyone that particular group might not feel are &quot;real&quot; Garou, and the Rite of Sacred Rebirth could be used to create loyal Garou.<br /> <br /> In any case, the PCs stumble across this situation, and then they need to decide how to deal with it. How do they learn the Rite is being used, and these new Garou aren't just Lost Cubs or late changers. How do they go about convincing other Garou this is the case? How do they rally other septs and organize a concolation to deal with it. A lot can be done with this kind of plot.<br /> <br /> This kind of thinking is completely mad, but as a lone exception it could be a great plot for the ST. Just because the vast majority of the Garou Nation will reject this doesn't mean every Garou will do so. I think it'd actually be a very fun plot to play through for players. The ST just needs to make sure this is an exception for a small group of Garou who have gone over the edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-19T18:25:33-08:00","id":1557769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557619#post1557619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if the idea is that Garou teach the Rite of Sacred Rebirth to kinfolk for the purposes of hunting Black Spiral Dancers and enabling them to become Garou, the big problem with that strategy is that you let the cat out of the bag. There is nothing to stop those kinfolk from turning on you. As a general idea, this is just bad.<br /> <br /> However, there's plenty of evidence of Garou being stupid and some Garou willing to deal with Wyrm minions for the purposes of fighting the greater evil. As such, I do think there's sufficient evidence to justify an ST for using this as a plot element in their chronicle if they wish.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, who said anything about &quot;teaching&quot; the rite to kinfolks? <br /> <br /> A sept could discreetly be on the lookout for kinfolks they consider good potential for the rite, then, once they have enough pelt from killed enemies, they could gather their prospects and do the rite on them. <br /> <br /> In such a scenario, kinfolks don't have the rite, it'd be the sole domain of the sept's theurges. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-20T11:53:36-08:00","id":1557785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557769#post1557769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, who said anything about &quot;teaching&quot; the rite to kinfolks?<br /> <br /> A sept could discreetly be on the lookout for kinfolks they consider good potential for the rite, then, once they have enough pelt from killed enemies, they could gather their prospects and do the rite on them.<br /> <br /> In such a scenario, kinfolks don't have the rite, it'd be the sole domain of the sept's theurges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Samuel learned the rite from the Verbena, who I believe are also the ones who invented it.<br /> <br /> Which lines up with the mythology about skin walkers being witches that turned to dark magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-20T18:18:17-08:00","id":1557793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557769#post1557769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In such a scenario, kinfolks don't have the rite, it'd be the sole domain of the sept's theurges.</div> </div> </div> </div>As written, the Rite is meant to be performed by a Kinfolk as ritemaster as the ritemaster himself is transformed. The rite is not something others do for someone else. It's a rite meant to be used by kinfolk, not Garou.<br /> <br /> Of course, STs can always change that if they want for their own chronicles. However, the canonical rite cannot be used in the way you mentioned.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-20T23:53:39-08:00","id":1557794,"title":"","content":"I think in this scenario the &quot;chosen one&quot; Kinfolks who would be &quot;gifted&quot; to become Garou with the Rite would be more indoctrinated than your everage cub in the Sept boot camp after their First Change to ensure loyalty <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 01-21-2026, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-22T22:24:16-08:00","id":1557849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557794#post1557794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in this scenario the &quot;chosen one&quot; Kinfolks who would be &quot;gifted&quot; to become Garou with the Rite would be more indoctrinated than your everage cub in the Sept boot camp after their First Change to ensure loyalty <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how most tribes treated their kinfolk? I don't think indoctrination would be necessary. They'd probably be so desperate to improve their lot in life, they'd jump at the chance as soon as it was presented.<br /> <br /> The Garou Nation was not exactly a friendly place. As evidenced by the fact pack leaders were commonly the most psychotic and aggressive members on the team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-24T23:17:47-08:00","id":1557890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557794#post1557794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in this scenario the &quot;chosen one&quot; Kinfolks who would be &quot;gifted&quot; to become Garou with the Rite would be more indoctrinated than your everage cub in the Sept boot camp after their First Change to ensure loyalty <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Somewhat related to the quoite topic I actually saw a Kinflok focused fan book called <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/en/product/547100/kinfolk-revisited?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Kinfolk revised</a> that actually offer at least three alternative ways to convert a kin into a garou that are relatively more Ethical than the Skin walker ritual.<br /> <br /> Which are A) the Bite which is ported from By Nights Studio version of WtA. That involves a garou biting a kinfolk and infecting them with a supernatural sickness that after a month would turn into a normal if steral garou. The bitten are are treated as a third breed with some stigma attached to them. Though not as strong as the crinos-born.<br /> <br /> B) Rite of Phoebe\u2019s Blossom which is Somewhat similar to the bite. Main difference is that the garou has to apply transformation inhibiting Mariphasa Ointment on to them selves as part of the rite and that the prospective kinfolk must have little knowledge (as opposed to the bite where any kinfolk or late bloomer's or Unborn could be turned) of the garou and they ways for the the rite to work on them (Do note the rite could work on a more expranced Knfolk, Though with a higher chance of complications such as spetrual and or mental imbalances). Which uh lead some obvious moral concerns.<br /> <br /> D) The Rite of Inheriting the Wolf which is relatively simpler to the above two where a kinflok was taken to a site of a recent battle to commune with the souls of the slain garous and Inherit they power to awaken as a full garou to take the place of the slain with a some what lopsided conversion rate (around 2 garou for 1 kinfolk).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 01-25-2026, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-25T01:11:52-08:00","id":1557891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557890#post1557890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Which are A) the Bite which is ported from By Nights Studio version of WtA. That involves a garou biting a kinfolk and infecting them with a supernatural sickness that after a month would turn into a normal if steral garou. The bitten are are treated as a third breed with some stigma attached to them. Though not as strong as the crinos-born.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, the Metamorphic Plague that effected the Black Furies potnetially could do such thing<br /> I mean it was - contrary of popular belief of the Garou - a Wyld &quot;Plague&quot; and not originated from the Wyrm. It not only had and affect on the infected's psyche - altered a fundamental principle within the person dramatically, like turns a 180 degree arc on it and altered Personalities and Memories - but also some cases changed the gender. It caused unpredictable physical mutations (causing a rise in male non-metis members within the tribe) also caused instability in shape-shifting.<br /> So basically side effect of Wyld energy exposure (or the will of the Wyld, tho' it is too chaotic and probably forgot it an instant; Delirium come to mind from Neil Gaiman' Sandman...) <br /> <br /> It is not that far-fetched the Metamorphic Plague or a mutated or, heck why not, Wyrm or Gaia-effected variant of it had a strange effect on Kinfolks turning them into a Garou<br /> <br /> Or, Minotaur would have a hand in such strange Phenomenon<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-25T04:30:27-08:00","id":1557893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557891#post1557891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, the Metamorphic Plague that effected the Black Furies potnetially could do such thing<br /> I mean it was - contrary of popular belief of the Garou - a Wyld &quot;Plague&quot; and not originated from the Wyrm. It not only had and affect on the infected's psyche - altered a fundamental principle within the person dramatically, like turns a 180 degree arc on it and altered Personalities and Memories - but also some cases changed the gender. It caused unpredictable physical mutations (causing a rise in male non-metis members within the tribe) also caused instability in shape-shifting.<br /> So basically side effect of Wyld energy exposure (or the will of the Wyld, tho' it is too chaotic and probably forgot it an instant; Delirium come to mind from Neil Gaiman' Sandman...)<br /> <br /> It is not that far-fetched the Metamorphic Plague or a mutated or, heck why not, Wyrm or Gaia-effected variant of it had a strange effect on Kinfolks turning them into a Garou<br /> <br /> Or, Minotaur would have a hand in such strange Phenomenon<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe though the cause seem to be linked general umbral instability caused by the BNS version of the apocalypse, where the worst adverted by the sacrifice of the garou king, so the mundane world is mostly fine though nearly all the ceanrs was ruined and the old rites need to create new ones are ueless. Add to that a surge of late bloomers or Unborns and the BSDs deciding to use the bite to create Furry shorvel heads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T18:02:25-08:00","id":1557935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557794#post1557794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in this scenario the &quot;chosen one&quot; Kinfolks who would be &quot;gifted&quot; to become Garou with the Rite would be more indoctrinated than your everage cub in the Sept boot camp after their First Change to ensure loyalty <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indoctrinated, but not so much that they would accept becoming Garou by a rite that would be considered not just criminal, but treasonous and blasphemous? You're carving out a very big exception to the rules there. One that would cause other Garou to not just kill them, but to execute the real Garou who were responsible for them. So how would they really react to their situation? Or if they are fine with that &quot;exception&quot;, then what other exceptions in Garou tradition are they also going to ignore?<br /> <br /> I think any loyal kinfolk who starts their life as a Garou through such a criminal act is going to have a lot of problems justifying to themselves.<br /> <br /> Even if we say that they were lied to about the nature of the Rite, they'll quickly learn that all other Garou consider it a horrible act and then what?<br /> <br /> The original Skin Dancers of Sam Haight had the excuse that they simply wanted the power of the Garou, and they weren't pretending they had any noble intent. They didn't have to reconcile their desire to be Garou and their loyalty to the Garou Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T23:44:39-08:00","id":1557940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557935#post1557935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indoctrinated, but not so much that they would accept becoming Garou by a rite that would be considered not just criminal, but treasonous and blasphemous? You're carving out a very big exception to the rules there. One that would cause other Garou to not just kill them, but to execute the real Garou who were responsible for them. So how would they really react to their situation? Or if they are fine with that &quot;exception&quot;, then what other exceptions in Garou tradition are they also going to ignore?<br /> <br /> I think any loyal kinfolk who starts their life as a Garou through such a criminal act is going to have a lot of problems justifying to themselves.<br /> <br /> Even if we say that they were lied to about the nature of the Rite, they'll quickly learn that all other Garou consider it a horrible act and then what?<br /> <br /> The original Skin Dancers of Sam Haight had the excuse that they simply wanted the power of the Garou, and they weren't pretending they had any noble intent. They didn't have to reconcile their desire to be Garou and their loyalty to the Garou Nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also I hlighted a Fan supplement that offer much more &quot;Legal&quot; ways of converting kinfolks into Garous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1556500-minotaur-as-an-enemy-faction-in-werewolf?p=1557890#post1557890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which are A) the Bite which is ported from By Nights Studio version of WtA. That involves a garou biting a kinfolk and infecting them with a supernatural sickness that after a month would turn into a normal if steral garou. The bitten are are treated as a third breed with some stigma attached to them. Though not as strong as the crinos-born.<br /> <br /> B) Rite of Phoebe\u2019s Blossom which is Somewhat similar to the bite. Main difference is that the garou has to apply transformation inhibiting Mariphasa Ointment on to them selves as part of the rite and that the prospective kinfolk must have little knowledge (as opposed to the bite where any kinfolk or late bloomer's or Unborn could be turned) of the garou and they ways for the the rite to work on them (Do note the rite could work on a more expranced Knfolk, Though with a higher chance of complications such as spetrual and or mental imbalances). Which uh lead some obvious moral concerns.<br /> <br /> D) The Rite of Inheriting the Wolf which is relatively simpler to the above two where a kinflok was taken to a site of a recent battle to commune with the souls of the slain garous and Inherit they power to awaken as a full garou to take the place of the slain with a some what lopsided conversion rate (around 2 garou for 1 kinfolk).</div> </div> </div> </div>A) &amp; D) are leagues more ethical than the Skin dancer Rite. With B) being disqualified for it's obvious iffy implications and D) being most socially acceptable option with the on;y obvious draw backs of needing a battle field of slain garous and a garou needing to preform the rite. Though a lenient ST can allow a kinfolk to preform rite since Kinfolks in this book are much more capable in canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}